    "passages": [
      {
        "id": "sha256:2e278f84e23b5bece931fb3971ab3747225a9a290995516afbbdfe2c510a3ea9",
        "source_id": "ORIGINAL-0001",
        "path": "original-0001.html",
        "hash": "sha256:93d03d3493443fc88a7926765b45deac1cfc15592e9bf03cc27b5a2c737fe124",
        "body_start": 2984,
        "text": "Much more polished is his printed Order of the Day for June 6, 1944, which Eisenhower began drafting in February. The order was distributed to the 175,000-member expeditionary force on the eve of the invasion.",
        "body_projection": "body-text-no-headings-v1",
        "context_truncated": false,
        "retrieval_score": 11.362988815737317
      },
      {
        "id": "sha256:6fb1563d468a869c67bdb744146038b18bf72fd3745643a7791bdd4fe3dd93fc",
        "source_id": "ORIGINAL-0003",
        "path": "original-0003.html",
        "hash": "sha256:0b85c918a8ebb763e38521d95e79e8d65d80d3c5d2667c14d2992a8d13e92b69",
        "body_start": 7529,
        "text": "Done at the City of Washington, this first day of January, in the year of our Lord one thousand eight hundred and sixty three, and of the Independence of the United States of America the eighty-seventh.",
        "body_projection": "body-text-no-headings-v1",
        "context_truncated": false,
        "retrieval_score": 6.939572174153316
      },
      {
        "id": "sha256:1040a318bad0e7a78c94698e0e0fb49fd9c91c4499968d5245b4b87d63b6640f",
        "source_id": "ORIGINAL-0002",
        "path": "original-0002.html",
        "hash": "sha256:2b2900e5cc6ad6fbcf9027310ff7ea41568a67df84a51a8f72352e1945ef85a4",
        "body_start": 9385,
        "text": "Attend an Event",
        "body_projection": "body-text-no-headings-v1",
        "context_truncated": false,
        "retrieval_score": 6.432123079854589
      },
      {
        "id": "sha256:e7f4edf1cccc602b468fde3c3aef5504e660cb75992297e48622a87e113eed66",
        "source_id": "ORIGINAL-0001",
        "path": "original-0001.html",
        "hash": "sha256:93d03d3493443fc88a7926765b45deac1cfc15592e9bf03cc27b5a2c737fe124",
        "body_start": 244,
        "text": "Home > General Dwight D. Eisenhower's Order of the Day (1944)",
        "body_projection": "body-text-no-headings-v1",
        "context_truncated": false,
        "retrieval_score": 10.81624975848396
      },
      {
        "id": "sha256:0cb626ee53f8b1b9b6aa7c41332d3052137d7e0b04a84dcebd1a58f2b10c31e3",
        "source_id": "ORIGINAL-0003",
        "path": "original-0003.html",
        "hash": "sha256:0b85c918a8ebb763e38521d95e79e8d65d80d3c5d2667c14d2992a8d13e92b69",
        "body_start": 8580,
        "text": "Attend an Event",
        "body_projection": "body-text-no-headings-v1",
        "context_truncated": false,
        "retrieval_score": 6.432123079854589
      },
      {
        "id": "sha256:6b60c29b730218f932d5b8cd37c53b424c591c71eecf143415fa358791f01f34",
        "source_id": "ORIGINAL-0002",
        "path": "original-0002.html",
        "hash": "sha256:2b2900e5cc6ad6fbcf9027310ff7ea41568a67df84a51a8f72352e1945ef85a4",
        "body_start": 5701,
        "text": "At the Second Session, Begun and held at the City of Washington, on Monday, the Fourth day of December, one thousand eight hundred and seventy-one.",
        "body_projection": "body-text-no-headings-v1",
        "context_truncated": false,
        "retrieval_score": 6.059662914274652
      },
      {
        "id": "sha256:6350a86b69cadcf7932a671510728f6fc016ddefcf600793188b62e08bb530fd",
        "source_id": "ORIGINAL-0001",
        "path": "original-0001.html",
        "hash": "sha256:93d03d3493443fc88a7926765b45deac1cfc15592e9bf03cc27b5a2c737fe124",
        "body_start": 674,
        "text": "This order was issued by Gen. Dwight D. Eisenhower to encourage Allied soldiers taking part in the D-day invasion.",
        "body_projection": "body-text-no-headings-v1",
        "context_truncated": false,
        "retrieval_score": 8.290153067991843
      },
      {
        "id": "sha256:0cd7ed0207b1842a0c0ecf6b33e4b688af74e6a79aed483104849df6411ecc79",
        "source_id": "ORIGINAL-0003",
        "path": "original-0003.html",
        "hash": "sha256:0b85c918a8ebb763e38521d95e79e8d65d80d3c5d2667c14d2992a8d13e92b69",
        "body_start": 4989,
        "text": "Now, therefore I, Abraham Lincoln, President of the United States, by virtue of the power in me vested as Commander-in-Chief, of the Army and Navy of the United States in time of actual armed rebellion against the authority and government of the United States, and as a fit and necessary war measure for suppressing said rebellion, do, on this first day of January, in the year of our Lord one thousand eight hundred and sixty-three, and in accordance with my purpose so to do publicly proclaimed for the full period of one hundred days, from the day first above mentioned, order and designate as the States and parts of States wherein the people thereof respectively, are this day in rebellion against the United States, the following, to wit:",
        "body_projection": "body-text-no-headings-v1",
        "context_truncated": false,
        "retrieval_score": 5.697068955536219
      },
      {
        "id": "sha256:703cfb0638272036066a3fe7549dcf72abd6c86fe2e47388fba204358730c3df",
        "source_id": "ORIGINAL-0001",
        "path": "original-0001.html",
        "hash": "sha256:93d03d3493443fc88a7926765b45deac1cfc15592e9bf03cc27b5a2c737fe124",
        "body_start": 5662,
        "text": "Attend an Event",
        "body_projection": "body-text-no-headings-v1",
        "context_truncated": false,
        "retrieval_score": 6.432123079854589
      },
      {
        "id": "sha256:99861267a0d05134b4363b6e6a8c49f4b8ae243746b34a5ab64a6dbfabc7a9eb",
        "source_id": "ORIGINAL-0003",
        "path": "original-0003.html",
        "hash": "sha256:0b85c918a8ebb763e38521d95e79e8d65d80d3c5d2667c14d2992a8d13e92b69",
        "body_start": 3502,
        "text": "Whereas, on the twenty-second day of September, in the year of our Lord one thousand eight hundred and sixty-two, a proclamation was issued by the President of the United States, containing, among other things, the following, to wit:",
        "body_projection": "body-text-no-headings-v1",
        "context_truncated": false,
        "retrieval_score": 3.8009966096835863
      },
      {
        "id": "sha256:3b9da9ad0de20bfc98ada546a7f53a166b35786fa9d466e3a16d096ba6ead0da",
        "source_id": "ORIGINAL-0001",
        "path": "original-0001.html",
        "hash": "sha256:93d03d3493443fc88a7926765b45deac1cfc15592e9bf03cc27b5a2c737fe124",
        "body_start": 354,
        "text": "Citation: D-day statement to soldiers, sailors, and airmen of the Allied Expeditionary Force, 6/44, Collection DDE-EPRE: Eisenhower, Dwight D: Papers, Pre-Presidential, 1916-1952; Dwight D. Eisenhower Library; National Archives and Records Administration.",
        "body_projection": "body-text-no-headings-v1",
        "context_truncated": false,
        "retrieval_score": 4.370910998067994
      },
      {
        "id": "sha256:2ce805b3ee10d88b7cd1632efb1105d5689e89e6dd27babef47a51cc468eb738",
        "source_id": "ORIGINAL-0003",
        "path": "original-0003.html",
        "hash": "sha256:0b85c918a8ebb763e38521d95e79e8d65d80d3c5d2667c14d2992a8d13e92b69",
        "body_start": 3736,
        "text": "\"That on the first day of January, in the year of our Lord one thousand eight hundred and sixty-three, all persons held as slaves within any State or designated part of a State, the people whereof shall then be in rebellion against the United States, shall be then, thenceforward, and forever free; and the Executive Government of the United States, including the military and naval authority thereof, will recognize and maintain the freedom of such persons, and will do no act or acts to repress such persons, or any of them, in any efforts they may make for their actual freedom.",
        "body_projection": "body-text-no-headings-v1",
        "context_truncated": false,
        "retrieval_score": 3.6843309697673794
      }
    ],
